    master: {
      heading: "Master revision table - Palliative symptom control and morphine",
      columns: ["Aspect", "High-yield points"],
      rows: [
        ["Definition", "**Active holistic care of people with serious health-related suffering** from severe illness and their families (IAHPC 2018) - based on **need, not prognosis**; neither hastens nor postpones death; starts early alongside disease treatment."],
        ["Relevant classification", "Pain: **nociceptive somatic, visceral, neuropathic, mixed**; breakthrough: incident, end-of-dose, spontaneous; **WHO ladder** (Step 1 NRS 1-3, Step 2 4-6, Step 3 7-10, adjuvants any step); **total pain** (physical, psychological, social, spiritual); ECOG / PPS."],
        ["Pathophysiology", "Tissue injury -> A-delta/C fibres -> dorsal horn -> **NMDA wind-up** (central sensitisation); morphine -> **mu receptor** -> less transmitter release; **M6G/M3G accumulate in renal failure** -> myoclonus, drowsiness; myenteric mu -> constipation (**no tolerance**)."],
        ["Key history (OPD)", "**ESAS-r** (4-6 moderate, 7-10 severe); history of **each pain** - mechanism chooses drug; rescue doses used per 24 h; opioid side effects; **red flags** (cord compression, hypercalcaemia, SVC); opiophobia; preferred place of care; PAINAD in dementia."],
        ["Key examination", "Each pain site; **rectal exam before escalating laxatives**; opioid toxicity signs (pinpoint pupils, **myoclonus**, RR under 8); leg neurology in back pain; mouth (thrush); pressure areas; palpable bladder in restlessness; PPS."],
        ["Minimal investigations", "Only if result changes care. **Creatinine/eGFR** before opioid choice (under 30 - avoid morphine, codeine); **corrected calcium** (Ca + 0.8 x (4 - albumin)); electrolytes, glucose; **whole-spine MRI within 24 h** for suspected MSCC."],
        ["Treatment - first line", "**Paracetamol 1 g 6-hourly** (3 g if frail); NSAID with PPI if no renal risk; **oral IR morphine 5-10 mg every 4 h** (2.5-5 mg if frail/renal), **double dose at bedtime**; **rescue = one-sixth of 24 h dose, hourly**; **senna 15 mg at night from first dose**."],
        ["Treatment - escalation", "Every 24-48 h add regular + rescue doses and redistribute; **max 30-50% rise per step**; convert to **MR = 24 h total / 2, 12-hourly**; **no ceiling dose**; switching opioids - **reduce 25-50%**; eGFR under 30 - fentanyl or buprenorphine patch."],
        ["Adjuvants", "Neuropathic - **gabapentin 300-600 mg TDS**, pregabalin, amitriptyline 10-25 mg, duloxetine; **dexamethasone 8 mg** (nerve/capsule), **16 mg** (cord compression) before noon with PPI; bone - **zoledronic acid 4 mg** or denosumab 120 mg, **single 8 Gy radiotherapy**."],
        ["Antiemetics by cause", "Chemical (opioid, uraemia, Ca) - **haloperidol 0.5-1.5 mg**; gastric stasis - **metoclopramide 10 mg TDS**; vestibular/raised ICP/obstruction - **cyclizine 50 mg TDS**; chemo - ondansetron; refractory - **levomepromazine 6.25 mg**; MBO - **octreotide 300-600 microgram + hyoscine butylbromide 60-120 mg/24 h**."],
        ["Devices / procedures", "**Oral to SC morphine 2:1**; syringe driver 24 h mix of 2-3 drugs in **water for injection** (cyclizine precipitates in saline); 24-25G butterfly in chest/arm/abdomen; check site 4-hourly, re-site 3-4 days; **SC rescue = one-sixth of 24 h SC dose**; no driver - 4-hourly SC boluses through butterfly."],
        ["Last days", "Breathlessness - fan, **morphine 2.5-5 mg PO / 1-2 mg SC**, lorazepam 0.5-1 mg SL; delirium - **haloperidol 0.5-1 mg**, terminal agitation **midazolam 10-30 mg/24 h**; death rattle - **hyoscine butylbromide 20 mg SC** or glycopyrronium 200 microgram early; mouth care; stop routine bloods."],
        ["Fentanyl and buprenorphine patches", "**Fentanyl 12 microgram/h = 30-45 mg oral morphine/day**, 25 = 60-90 mg; change **72-hourly**, onset 12-24 h, stable pain only, **never opioid-naive**, heat increases absorption; **buprenorphine 5 microgram/h = about 12 mg morphine**, 7-day patch, safe in renal failure."],
        ["Complications and emergencies", "**MSCC** - dexamethasone 16 mg now, MRI 24 h; **SVC obstruction** - dexamethasone, stent; **hypercalcaemia** - saline 2-4 L + zoledronic acid 4 mg; **catastrophic bleed** - dark towels, midazolam 10 mg; **opioid toxicity** - naloxone 20 microgram IV steps."],
        ["Red flags and referral", "RR under 8 with unrousable sedation; new myoclonus (renal decline); back pain + leg weakness; confusion + polyuria; facial swelling; absolute constipation with vomiting; pain escalating despite titration - specialist palliative team."],
        ["Follow-up and monitoring", "Review **24-72 h** after starting/changing morphine, then weekly while titrating; ESAS target **3 or less**; recheck creatinine if myoclonus or drowsiness; taper dexamethasone weekly; bereavement contact; **take back unused opioids**."],
        ["Prevention / national programme", "**NPPC 2012** under NHM; Kerala Neighbourhood Network model; **NDPS Amendment Act 2014** - essential narcotic drugs, **one RMI approval** from State Drugs Controller (Rules 2015); oral morphine on **NLEM 2022**; palliative care in Ayushman Arogya Mandir package."],
        ["Latest guideline change", "No change needed - WHO 2018 cancer pain guideline, PCF and NICE NG234 (MSCC, 2023) remain current; Indian access rules unchanged since the 2014-2015 NDPS amendments."],
        ["Exam one-liners", "Rescue = one-sixth of 24 h dose. Oral:SC morphine 2:1. Never an opioid without a stimulant laxative. Sedation precedes respiratory depression. Fan plus low-dose morphine beats oxygen for the non-hypoxic."],
      ],
    },
